WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.922
Once upon a time there was a small village deep in the mountains.

2
00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:14.025
To visitors, the village looked peaceful and beautiful.

3
00:00:16.326 --> 00:00:19.769
However the people in the village were very afraid.

4
00:00:20.309 --> 00:00:23.131
They were afraid of the tigers living in the mountains.

5
00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.736
The people in the village went into the mountains to hunt for food.

6
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:32.310
But the tigers did not like that.

7
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.612
The tigers frightened and chased the people out.

8
00:00:37.474 --> 00:00:39.416
The village decided to hold a meeting.

9
00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:42.658
They wanted to get rid of the tigers in the mountains.

10
00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:45.821
"We are tired of living in fear!"

11
00:00:46.541 --> 00:00:47.462
shouted one man.

12
00:00:47.482 --> 00:00:51.325
"What if the tigers come to our village and eat our children?"

13
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:52.506
cried a woman.

14
00:00:54.108 --> 00:00:56.009
Finally a young man stood up.

15
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.272
"We must make a trap to catch the tigers!"

16
00:00:59.904 --> 00:01:00.445
he said.

17
00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:02.666
"What kind of trap?"

18
00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:04.467
asked another man.

19
00:01:04.487 --> 00:01:07.269
"We must dig very deep holes.

20
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:12.893
The tigers will fall into them, but they will not be able to climb out," said the young

21
00:01:12.933 --> 00:01:16.236
man. Everyone cheered at the wonderful idea.

22
00:01:19.318 --> 00:01:22.120
The village worked day and night digging holes.

23
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.263
They dug holes around the village and up the road to the mountain.

24
00:01:26.963 --> 00:01:28.124
At last they were done.

25
00:01:30.252 --> 00:01:32.614
One day a traveler was passing by the village.

26
00:01:33.474 --> 00:01:37.237
As he walked by a big hole in the ground, he heard a low roar.

27
00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.339
The traveler stopped and looked down the hole.

28
00:01:43.021 --> 00:01:44.982
At the bottom of the hole was a tiger!

29
00:01:45.002 --> 00:01:49.705
"Oh please, kind sir, help me!"

30
00:01:51.106 --> 00:01:52.027
begged the tiger.

31
00:01:52.047 --> 00:01:57.370
"I promise never to forget your kindness if only you will help me!"

32
00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.392
cried the tiger.

33
00:02:00.992 --> 00:02:03.233
The traveler felt sorry for the tiger.

34
00:02:03.974 --> 00:02:07.236
He dragged a felled tree and lowered it into the hole.

35
00:02:08.036 --> 00:02:09.937
The tiger climbed out of the trap.

36
00:02:09.957 --> 00:02:15.560
"Thank you for your kindness," said the tiger.

37
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.902
"And now, I am going to eat you."

38
00:02:18.922 --> 00:02:20.583
"But why?

39
00:02:21.103 --> 00:02:22.504
I just saved your life!"

40
00:02:23.124 --> 00:02:24.085
cried the traveler.

41
00:02:24.105 --> 00:02:31.137
"Because humans made those traps to catch tigers, and you are a human," said the tiger.

42
00:02:33.598 --> 00:02:36.540
The man was very frightened, but he had an idea.

43
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.422
"It's not fair, Mr.

44
00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:44.866
Tiger, to judge one person the same as everyone else," the man said bravely.

45
00:02:44.886 --> 00:02:49.609
"Let's hear what others have to say about this situation."

46
00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.632
The tiger agreed and the two of them set off.

47
00:02:54.993 --> 00:02:57.015
The man and the tiger went to an ox.

48
00:02:57.535 --> 00:02:58.736
They told him what happened.

49
00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:04.842
After listening the ox said, "Well, I have to agree with the tiger.

50
00:03:05.102 --> 00:03:06.622
Humans are cruel and mean.

51
00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:09.843
They tie us up and make us work hard all the time."

52
00:03:11.884 --> 00:03:14.024
Next they went to a pine tree.

53
00:03:14.704 --> 00:03:16.625
The pine tree listened to their story.

54
00:03:17.425 --> 00:03:21.606
Then it said, "Well, I have to agree with the tiger.

55
00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:23.227
Humans are unkind!

56
00:03:23.687 --> 00:03:25.867
They cut us down and throw us into the fire.

57
00:03:26.268 --> 00:03:27.388
Humans have no heart!"

58
00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:29.860
"You see?

59
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.421
Humans are bad!

60
00:03:31.941 --> 00:03:35.522
Now, I'm going to eat you," the tiger said.

61
00:03:36.142 --> 00:03:39.803
The tiger was about to attack, when a rabbit came hopping by.

62
00:03:39.823 --> 00:03:43.264
"What's going on?"

63
00:03:43.564 --> 00:03:44.424
the rabbit asked.

64
00:03:44.444 --> 00:03:46.285
"Oh please, Mr.

65
00:03:46.365 --> 00:03:48.446
Rabbit," cried the traveler.

66
00:03:48.946 --> 00:03:50.506
"Listen and judge our case."

67
00:03:50.526 --> 00:03:56.348
"Fine, but we must hop back to where this all started," answered the rabbit.

68
00:03:58.112 --> 00:04:00.593
"Where were you before this human rescued you?"

69
00:04:01.213 --> 00:04:02.613
the rabbit asked the tiger.

70
00:04:03.393 --> 00:04:04.874
The tiger pointed to the trap.

71
00:04:04.894 --> 00:04:09.275
"I must see exactly where you were," said the rabbit.

72
00:04:10.235 --> 00:04:12.336
So the tiger jumped into the deep hole.

73
00:04:13.896 --> 00:04:17.217
"Was this felled tree in the hole when you fell into it, Mr.

74
00:04:17.277 --> 00:04:18.898
Tiger?" asked the rabbit.

75
00:04:18.918 --> 00:04:20.838
"No, no.

76
00:04:21.378 --> 00:04:24.579
There was nothing here," answered the tiger.

77
00:04:25.219 --> 00:04:27.720
So the traveler and the rabbit pulled the tree out.

78
00:04:29.392 --> 00:04:32.754
"You were trapped in this hole, with no one to help you.

79
00:04:34.415 --> 00:04:40.137
Then this kind man comes along and helps you, and now you want to kill him?

80
00:04:41.098 --> 00:04:42.779
That is not kind, Mr.

81
00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:44.580
Tiger," said the rabbit.

82
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.902
"You complain that humans are unkind, but you are not being fair.

83
00:04:50.503 --> 00:04:53.124
You must not judge someone you have never met."

84
00:04:57.441 --> 00:05:00.349
The tiger remained ungrateful to the man who saved his life.

85
00:05:00.931 --> 00:05:05.223
So the traveler and the rabbit left the tiger in the hole and walked away.
